sequenceDiagram
  participant User as Staff / Student
  participant BFF as Next.js BFF
  participant Client as Staff API client
  participant API as Spring Identity API
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  alt Student sign-in (no MFA unless the student set one up)
    User->>BFF: Login credentials over HTTPS
    BFF->>API: POST /auth/login
    API->>DB: Check password, account status and lockout
    API-->>BFF: Access JWT and opaque refresh token
    BFF-->>User: HttpOnly SameSite session cookies
    User->>BFF: Protected request with session cookie
    Note over User,BFF: BFF checks Origin on mutations
    BFF->>API: Bearer JWT on server-side request
  else Staff sign-in, every staff role (001G; all roles since FIX-3)
    User->>BFF: Login credentials over HTTPS
    BFF->>API: POST /auth/login
    API->>DB: Check password and store challenge digest
    API-->>BFF: MFA challenge with enrolment status
    BFF-->>User: Sealed HttpOnly MFA challenge cookie, redirect to /sign-in/mfa
    opt First sign-in or authenticator reset
      BFF->>API: POST /auth/mfa/enroll with challenge
      API->>DB: Store encrypted authenticator secret
      API-->>BFF: Setup secret and authenticator URI
      BFF-->>User: QR code and manual setup secret
    end
    User->>BFF: Verification or recovery code (POST /api/session/mfa-verify)
    BFF->>API: POST /auth/mfa/verify with challenge and code
    API->>DB: Verify factor, consume challenge and start MFA session
    API-->>BFF: Access JWT, refresh token and recovery codes on enrolment
    opt First sign-in: recovery codes presentation
      BFF-->>User: Sealed recovery cookie, redirect to /sign-in/mfa/recovery-codes
      User->>BFF: Acknowledge recovery codes (POST /api/session/mfa-recovery)
      BFF-->>User: Clear recovery cookie, redirect to /staff
    end
    BFF-->>User: HttpOnly SameSite session cookies, redirect to /staff
  end
  API->>API: Check token, session, privileged MFA, roles and resource scope
  Note over BFF,API: Refresh rotates the opaque token and reuse revokes the session
